# lisp-d: d in Clojure (#428). A call through a namespace alias lands on its `defn` in the file of
# the namespace the `ns` form requires, and a `let` binding is local. The files are written here,
# not in the project, which every other scenario counts the files of.
merl
wait Open a file (fuzzy)
run mkdir -p cljshop/src/shop && printf '(ns shop.money)\n\n(defn format-price [cents]\n  (format "$%%.2f" (/ cents 100.0)))\n' > cljshop/src/shop/money.clj && printf '(ns shop.cart\n  (:require [shop.money :as money]))\n\n(defn label [cart]\n  (let [total (reduce + cart)]\n    (str "Total: " (money/format-price total))))\n' > cljshop/src/shop/cart.clj
key q
wait merl exited: 0
merl cljshop/src/shop/cart.clj
wait (ns shop.cart
key /
type format-price total
key Enter d
wait format-price: via import
merl cljshop/src/shop/cart.clj
wait (ns shop.cart
key /
type total)
key Enter d
wait (local)
key Escape
